### Pre-outcome S1A benchmark-dependence reopening — public fixture distribution invalidates C1/C2 as advantage baselines

A second hostile review found another load-bearing issue **before any S1A result**.

The frozen eight marked positions per `n` are generated by a public deterministic rule/seed committed in the repository. A classical strategy with access to the published benchmark construction can precompute that eight-position support and query those locations first. Therefore the original C1 ordered scan / C2 random-permutation means are not the strongest classical comparator under all public benchmark side information.

This is not hypothetical: Pal/Sharma/Podila 2026 (`Loophole-Robust Certification of Quantum Advantage`, arXiv:2607.13090) formalize benchmark-correlated classical side resources and show that construction-side information can close apparent quantum/classical gaps.

**Pre-outcome correction:**

- retain the eight deterministic cases unchanged as **semantic/conformance fixtures only**;
- they may validate circuit semantics, actual measurement, retry/query accounting, backend identity, and P4 reconstruction;
- they may **not** supply the quantum-advantage comparator means;
- adjudicate `QUANTUM_QUERY_ADVANTAGE_ONLY` only in the explicitly registered standard unstructured query model with a hidden marked item uniformly distributed over all `N` positions;
- use the analytic quantum single-run success `p = sin^2((2r+1)theta)` and compare `r` coherent queries against the optimal no-side-information classical oracle-query requirement needed to attain the same verified success probability;
- preserve both worst/query-budget and expected classical-query coordinates;
- record `fixture_cases_used_for_advantage = false` and reject any artifact that changes it;
- ordinary classical-predicate input still remains `CANNOT_CHECK_ACCESS_MODEL` under the separate access amendment.

This makes the synthetic fixtures an implementation verifier, not an engineered distribution that can manufacture an advantage. The original S1A packet remains immutable history; a second additive amendment and RED→GREEN tests will encode this stronger gate before the first result-bearing run.
